    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d426">

                <pb facs="0541" n="531" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg531"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11–148: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ward</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-01">November 1,
                        1948</date>.<lb/>[Received November 1—3:23 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>474. 1510 hours Communist troops now in effective occupation of Mukden. Small
                    arms fire which has been going on within city since daylight has ceased.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 619; repeated Department 474, Peiping 245, Tientsin 161, Tsingtao
                    123.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ward</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
